{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"User Profiler API","version":"1.0.0"},"servers":[{"url":"/up"}],"paths":{"/api/v1":{"get":{"summary":"Api Home","operationId":"api_home_api_v1_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{}}}}}}},"/user/me/keywords":{"get":{"summary":"Keywords of the token's own user (UI profile page)","description":"Keywords stored in grafeo, with weight and \"expired\" flag. When there are none, status says why:\n    - \"ok\": keywords available\n    - \"pending\": a refresh from the DMM is running -> ask again in a few seconds\n    - \"no_queries\": the DMM has no queries for the user yet\n    - \"no_keywords\": the queries were processed, but no keywords came out\n    - \"error\": the last refresh failed (DMM or LLM); it is retried later\n    - \"no_profile\": the UP has no profile for this user yet\nA user without keywords gets a new refresh at most every KEYWORD_REFRESH_COOLDOWN_SECONDS\n(and always after a restart), so polling this endpoint is cheap.","operationId":"get_my_keywords_user_me_keywords_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MyKeywords"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]},{"OAuth2PasswordBearer":[]}]}},"/user/{user_id}/queries":{"post":{"summary":"Notify that the user has performed a new query (triggers a refresh)","description":"notify that the user has performed a new query\n    --> creates the user if the UP has never seen it, then triggers the refresh","operationId":"notify_query_user__user_id__queries_post","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]},{"OAuth2PasswordBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"user_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"User Id"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/QueryEvent"}}}},"responses":{"202":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema"